Adversarial auditor, round 3. Read-only on all source trees; writes only in `audit_hard_r3/leak_sweep/`. No number below is invented: every figure is quoted from a named file or measured by the saved probe.

## 1. VERDICT (3 lines)

Swept 66/66 `.py` files; the eval-corpus-fit recipe is project-wide (12 code files, all datasets) but no published number is overturned beyond round-2's known RealTalk-k96 collapse, so there is no new CRITICAL finding.
New probe D1 (n=705): BM25 with background IDF scores 55.18 vs 54.18 per-archive (+0.99 pp) — the transduction asymmetry favours the codes, so the STOP verdict survives and is, if anything, understated.
Zero fits on queries or gold anywhere; all leaks are docs-only index-time fits.

